  "note": "Election of the Lisburn Borough Council, May 1958: fifteen councillors in three wards. North and South Wards were polled on Wednesday 21 May 1958 (Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1958, p. 2); in Central Ward five candidates were returned unopposed for six seats (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6), the sixth seat's holder not being named in the sources read. No party labels are printed. Five nominations for six seats. Under the 1949 regulations (reg. 15(2)) the remaining seat went to a retiring member deemed re-elected, if one was eligible; no source read names him or her. Returned unopposed."
